# Code owners — review required on the files that do the enforcing.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The append-only guard reads its own GUARDED list from
# scripts/check-decisions-immutable.sh, and CI runs that script from the pull request's
# own branch. So a PR can delete a decision record and, in the same commit, edit the
# script so the check no longer looks at it — and the check passes. That edit is visible
# in the diff, but nothing forces anyone to look at it. This file forces the look.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE USING THE TEMPLATE ON A CLIENT REPO
# Replace @oneEyedBunny below with a handle that has write access to THAT repo. A
# CODEOWNERS entry naming someone without access cannot be satisfied — GitHub will block
# every pull request touching these paths and the reason is not obvious from the error.
# Wrong handle here is worse than no file.
#
# THIS FILE ALONE ENFORCES NOTHING.
# It only bites when branch protection is set to require review from code owners. That
# is a GitHub setting, not a file — see docs/handoff.md.

/.github/                       @oneEyedBunny
/scripts/                       @oneEyedBunny
